<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
This file defines the macro `plugin_linear_battery` that emits the XML for the
Gazebo Sim plugin `gz::sim::systems::LinearBatteryPlugin`.

The battery system keeps track of the battery charge on a robot model.
Currently, one battery per model is supported. When the battery drains
completely, all joints of the corresponding model are turned off, meaning joint
forces are set to 0.

To find the reference for the system Gazebo plugins:
1. Go to: https://gazebosim.org/libs/
2. Click in the link 'API & Tutorials' for the 'Sim' section.
3. Click in the link 'gz::sim::systems'

At the time of writing this text (June 2026), this workspace uses Gazebo Sim
8.11.0 through the ROS Jazzy `ros-jazzy-gz-sim-vendor` package.
The LinearBatteryPlugin reference is:
https://gazebosim.org/api/sim/8/classgz_1_1sim_1_1systems_1_1LinearBatteryPlugin.html

The battery tutorial with an SDF example is:
https://gazebosim.org/api/sim/8/battery.html

Parameters for a basic functional battery:
You do not need to set every parameter in this macro to get a functional battery.
The following parameters are enough to create a battery with a fixed voltage, a total charge, and a constant consumer
load:
- `name`: The name of the battery.
- `voltage`: Initial voltage of the battery in volts.
- `capacity`: Total charge that the battery can hold in ampere-hours.
- `power_load`: Power load on the battery in watts.
- `fix_issue_225`: Enables Gazebo's corrected battery state-of-charge behavior.
  Without this flag, Gazebo keeps the legacy behavior described in gz-sim issue 225, where the documented runtime
  calculation has to include a 100x drain-rate factor.
  See the `Runtime estimate` and `Known limitation` sections below.
  In Gazebo Sim 8.11.0 this flag is still read by the plugin source code, so the macro enables it by default.
  Use `fix_issue_225="false"` only if you intentionally need legacy battery behavior.
  Issue: https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/issues/225
  Source: https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/gz-sim8/src/systems/battery_plugin/LinearBatteryPlugin.cc

The battery state is published by Gazebo on:
`/model/<model_name>/battery/<battery_name>/state`

Runtime estimate:

  battery_runtime_hours = capacity_Ah * voltage_V / power_load_W

Known limitation:
- If `fix_issue_225` is not enabled on affected Gazebo versions, the battery can  drain at a 100x faster rate.
  In that case, the runtime estimate is:

  battery_runtime_hours = capacity_Ah * voltage_V / (power_load_W * 100)

Ideal battery with no discharge:
- If a robot needs a battery state topic but the battery should behave like an ideal infinite battery, use the same
  basic battery parameters and set `power_load` to 0.
- The important field is `power_load="0.0"`. With zero power load, the plugin can publish battery state while the stored
  charge remains constant.
- Keep `voltage` positive. Do not use `voltage="0.0"`, because the plugin computes current from power divided by
  voltage.
- The following configuration keeps the battery topic active and avoids discharge:

  <xacro:plugin_linear_battery
      name="main_battery"
      voltage="24.0"
      capacity="20.0"
      power_load="0.0"
  />

Parameters for a more realistic battery:
If you need to model a more realistic battery, use the basic battery parameters above and add any of the following
fields:
- `open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef`: Voltage at full charge in volts.
   If omitted, the macro uses the same value as `voltage`.
- `open_circuit_voltage_linear_coef`: Voltage decrease when the battery has no charge.
- `initial_charge`: Initial charge of the battery in ampere-hours.
- `resistance`: Internal resistance in ohms.
- `smooth_current_tau`: Coefficient for smoothing current.
- `invert_current_sign`: Flips the sign of the current reported in the battery state message.
- `start_draining`: Starts draining the battery at the beginning of the simulation.
- `power_draining_topic`: Topic that starts power draining when a message is received.
- `stop_power_draining_topic`: Topic that stops power draining when a message is received.

Charging:
- Whether the battery is modeled with only the basic parameters or with the more realistic parameters above, the
  following fields enable recharge behavior.
- `enable_recharge`: Enables battery recharging.
- `charging_time`: Hours needed to fully charge the battery with no load.
- `recharge_by_topic`: If true, the plugin also subscribes to Gazebo Transport message topics for starting and
  stopping recharge.
- When recharge is enabled, Gazebo always exposes these Gazebo Transport services. Both services use
  `gz::msgs::Boolean`:
  `/model/<model_name>/battery/<battery_name>/recharge/start`
  `/model/<model_name>/battery/<battery_name>/recharge/stop`
- If `recharge_by_topic` is true, the plugin also accepts `gz::msgs::Boolean` messages published on topics with those
  exact same names.
-->
<robot name="plugin_linear_battery_macro" xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro"
       xmlns:gz="http://gazebosim.org/schema">
  <xacro:macro name="plugin_linear_battery"
               params="name
                       voltage
                       capacity
                       power_load
                       fix_issue_225:=true
                       open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef:=''
                       open_circuit_voltage_linear_coef:=''
                       initial_charge:=''
                       resistance:=''
                       smooth_current_tau:=''
                       invert_current_sign:=''
                       start_draining:=''
                       power_draining_topic:=''
                       stop_power_draining_topic:=''
                       enable_recharge:=''
                       charging_time:=''
                       recharge_by_topic:=''">

    <xacro:if value="${fix_issue_225 not in (True, False)}">
      ${xacro.fatal("plugin_linear_battery: fix_issue_225 must be true or false")}
    </xacro:if>

    <xacro:if value="${invert_current_sign != '' and invert_current_sign not in (True, False)}">
      ${xacro.fatal("plugin_linear_battery: invert_current_sign must be true or false")}
    </xacro:if>

    <xacro:if value="${start_draining != '' and start_draining not in (True, False)}">
      ${xacro.fatal("plugin_linear_battery: start_draining must be true or false")}
    </xacro:if>

    <xacro:if value="${enable_recharge != '' and enable_recharge not in (True, False)}">
      ${xacro.fatal("plugin_linear_battery: enable_recharge must be true or false")}
    </xacro:if>

    <plugin filename="gz-sim-linearbatteryplugin-system" name="gz::sim::systems::LinearBatteryPlugin">
      <battery_name>${name}</battery_name>
      <voltage>${voltage}</voltage>
      <capacity>${capacity}</capacity>
      <power_load>${power_load}</power_load>

      <xacro:if value="${fix_issue_225 != ''}">
        <fix_issue_225>${fix_issue_225}</fix_issue_225>
      </xacro:if>

      <!--
      Gazebo's internal default for open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef is 0.0.
      Use the configured initial voltage when the caller does not set a more
      specific value, so the basic battery keeps that voltage while discharging.
      -->
      <xacro:if value="${open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef == ''}">
        <open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef>${voltage}</open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef != ''}">
        <open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef>${open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef}</open_circuit_voltage_constant_coef>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${open_circuit_voltage_linear_coef != ''}">
        <open_circuit_voltage_linear_coef>${open_circuit_voltage_linear_coef}</open_circuit_voltage_linear_coef>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${initial_charge != ''}">
        <initial_charge>${initial_charge}</initial_charge>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${resistance != ''}">
        <resistance>${resistance}</resistance>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${smooth_current_tau != ''}">
        <smooth_current_tau>${smooth_current_tau}</smooth_current_tau>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${invert_current_sign != ''}">
        <invert_current_sign>${invert_current_sign}</invert_current_sign>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${start_draining != ''}">
        <start_draining>${start_draining}</start_draining>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${power_draining_topic != ''}">
        <power_draining_topic>${power_draining_topic}</power_draining_topic>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${stop_power_draining_topic != ''}">
        <stop_power_draining_topic>${stop_power_draining_topic}</stop_power_draining_topic>
      </xacro:if>

      <xacro:if value="${enable_recharge != '' and enable_recharge}">
        <enable_recharge>${enable_recharge}</enable_recharge>

        <xacro:if value="${charging_time == ''}">
          ${xacro.fatal("plugin_linear_battery: charging_time is required when enable_recharge is true")}
        </xacro:if>

        <charging_time>${charging_time}</charging_time>

        <xacro:if value="${recharge_by_topic != '' and recharge_by_topic not in (True, False)}">
          ${xacro.fatal("plugin_linear_battery: recharge_by_topic must be true or false")}
        </xacro:if>

        <xacro:if value="${recharge_by_topic != '' and recharge_by_topic}">
          <recharge_by_topic>${recharge_by_topic}</recharge_by_topic>
        </xacro:if>
      </xacro:if>
    </plugin>
  </xacro:macro>
</robot>
